  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Simplify $\\left(\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{c}{d}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{a}{b}-\\frac{c}{d}\\right)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{ad+bc}{ad-bc}$",
      "worked": "Use the common denominator $bd$, then multiply by the reciprocal.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{c}{d}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{a}{b}-\\frac{c}{d}\\right)&=\\frac{ad+bc}{bd}\\div\\frac{ad-bc}{bd}\\\\\\left(\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{c}{d}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{a}{b}-\\frac{c}{d}\\right)&=\\frac{ad+bc}{bd}\\times\\frac{bd}{ad-bc}\\\\\\left(\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{c}{d}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{a}{b}-\\frac{c}{d}\\right)&=\\frac{ad+bc}{ad-bc}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $b\\ne0$, $d\\ne0$ and $ad-bc\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 39
  },
